{
 "description": "What the layered looks of MH4U cost in materials (core/equipment/layered/prices.py). 'rules': at most 'materials' materials and 'quantity' units of each in a recipe-based price, the hardest material of a large monster's look (an item of that monster's own drop lists), and when its best chance is above 'rare_percent' (it is not rare) the monster's next pick of that rank too, 'units_by_percent' how many units of a monster's material a look asks by its best chance ([bound, units] by rising bound: the first bound the chance does not pass), 'max_families' how many families may drop an item for a look to ask it (its own and one other at 2), 'rare_percent' the best chance (percent) up to which an item of the look's own rank is hard enough (above it, or without one, the look takes the rarest item that drops at its rank wherever the item belongs), 'min_share' the share of a recipe's units a family's exclusive materials must make for a look to be that family's (below it the look is no large monster's; inside the family it goes to the member whose own drops hold most of those units, a tie to the base). 'unobtainable': the item categories a player never holds, never asked by any rule (an event's ticket, an account item sold at the quest's end, what the wiki does not know). 'monster': a look's monster set by hand, where the rule cannot decide ('armor' / 'weapons': look key -> a large monster's name, or 'none' for no large monster). 'kiranico_names': Kiranico's monster name -> ours, where they differ. 'not_asked': a large monster's name -> the items its looks never ask though the rule would (what it drops for wearing another monster's skin). 'xx': which MH4U monster a look of MH XX is of (core/equipment/layered/xx_monsters.py, tools/build/build_layered_xx.py): 'words' a word of a set's name (lowercase) -> the monster it names, 'monster' a set's name -> [the monster or 'none', why] where the name does not say it (checked against the set's own recipe), 'rules' the recipe vote of the weapons: an item that more than 'series_max' armor series ask is common, a weapon is a monster's when the monster holds 'weapon_share' of its recipes' units of non-common items and the second monster at most 'weapon_lead' of the first's; 'recipe' the looks of no monster (xx_prices.recipe_records): they cost the first 'materials' of their recipe like MH4U's when MH4U has each of them by English name, an item of a category in 'unobtainable' counting as missing, 'names' an XX name -> MH4U's where they spell one item otherwise, 'replace' what an XX item MH4U lacks asks instead in such a recipe: 'items' an XX item's English name -> 'skip' (a ticket, a coin, an event's item: the next material counts), 'kind:K' (the item of 'kinds' K of the look's rank: [low, high, G], null skips it), 'monster:M' (the rare material monster M's look of that rank asks, its units by 'units_by_percent': MH4U's, an XX monster's of xx_materials.json, a ported one's) or an MH4U item's English name (a small monster's part: its MH4U relative).",
